SUMMARY:Deadline: Finnish Cultural Foundation: October Round 2026 (all fiel
 ds of art and science)
DESCRIPTION:Finland's largest private foundation moves to a single joint ap
 plication round in 2026: the central fund and all 17 regional funds accept
  applications together from 15 to 30 October. It funds all fields of art a
 nd science\, with one-year and multi-year working grants as the cornerston
 e alongside project grants for individuals\, working groups and organisati
 ons.\n\nOrganisation: Finnish Cultural Foundation (Suomen Kulttuurirahasto
 )\nLocation: Finland. Open to Finnish nationals\, people and organisations
  residing or working in Finland\, and other applicants with demonstrable s
 trong ties to Finland or Finnish culture.\nAward: Around EUR 49 million aw
 arded annually across roughly 2\,100 grants\; recent October rounds have a
 veraged over 450 working and project grants covering one or more years\, w
 ith working grants extending up to four years. No application fee.\nDurati
 on: Working grants of one to four years\; project grants per project\n\nMo
 re: https://skr.fi/en/grants/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_me
 dium=referral
URL:https://skr.fi/en/grants/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
LOCATION:Finland. Open to Finnish nationals\, people and organisations resi
 ding or working in Finland\, and other applicants with demonstrable strong
  ties to Finland or Finnish culture.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cerv-2026-citizens-rem@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261111T152048Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART:20270224T153000Z
DTEND:20270224T160000Z
SUMMARY:Deadline 17:00 CET: EU CERV: European Remembrance 2026-27 (CERV-202
 6-CITIZENS-REM)
DESCRIPTION:Closes 24 Feb 2027 at 17:00 CET.\n\nThe EU's main remembrance f
 unding line\, and emphatically not Holocaust-only: the 2026-27 call (cover
 ing both years\; there is no separate 2027 call) funds projects across fou
 r topics: 1) remembering democratic transitions and the (re)building of de
 mocratic institutions\; 2) remembrance of the Holocaust against Jewish peo
 ple\; 3) remembrance of the Holocaust\, acts of genocide\, war crimes and 
 crimes...\n\nOrganisation: European Commission / EACEA (Citizens\, Equalit
 y\, Rights and Values Programme)\nLocation: EU Member States (incl. OCTs) 
 and CERV-associated countries. Lead applicant must be a non-profit legal e
 ntity or international organisation.\nAward: EUR 50\,000 to EUR 500\,000 p
 er project\, from an estimated call budget of EUR 28 million (EUR 14M Holo
 caust remembrance of Jewish victims\; EUR 5M genocide\, war crimes and cri
