 me of the E.ON Foundation\, E-WERK Luckenwalde and Ujazdowski Castle Centr
 e for Contemporary Art (Warsaw).\n\nOrganisation: JUNGE AKADEMIE of the Ak
 ademie der Künste\, VISIT (E.ON Foundation)\, E-WERK Luckenwalde and Ujaz
 dowski Castle Centre for Contemporary Art\nLocation: E-WERK Luckenwalde\, 
 Brandenburg\, Germany (3 fellows) and Akademie der Künste\, Berlin (1 fel
 low)\, with a retreat at Ujazdowski Castle CCA in Warsaw\, Poland. Open to
  artists worldwide.\nAward: Four fully funded fellowships of EUR 20\,000 e
 ach\, intended for artist fees and production costs of a new project (rese
 arch and development\, travel\, materials and presentation costs)\, plus s
 tudio space and accommodation for the three-month residency.\nDuration: Ab
 out three months\, mid-August to mid-November 2027: retreat at Ujazdowski 
 Castle in Warsaw in mid-August\, then the residency at E-WERK Luckenwalde 
 or Akademie der Künste Berlin from late August\, ending with a symposium 
 at the Akademie der Künste on 5 and 6 November 2027. Fellows must be avai
 lable from 13 August to 10 November 2027 and live and work on site at leas
 t 75% of the time.\n\nMore: https://adk.de/news/2026/10/open-call-mensch-m
 aschine-stipendium?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referr
